From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] LinBox box64: static-binary exit fix backport (v0.3.0 layout)

Same backport as 0005 for the v0.3.0 emulate() layout: v0.3.0 has no { }
block around the entry setup and ends with Run(emu, 0) instead of
DynaRun(emu).

Anchor (3 lines):
    "Push64(emu, my_context->exit_bridge); ..." / "SetRDX(emu, Pop64(emu)); ..." /
    "Run(emu, 0);"
The trailing "Run(emu, 0);" exists ONLY in v0.3.0 (every later tag ends
emulate() with DynaRun(emu)), so this file is skipped everywhere else.
Requires 0001 (declares linbox_hasinterp); sort order applies it first.
---
diff --git a/src/core.c b/src/core.c
--- a/src/core.c
+++ b/src/core.c
@@ -2286,4 +2286,15 @@
     Push64(emu, my_context->exit_bridge);  // push to pop it just after
     SetRDX(emu, Pop64(emu));    // RDX is exit function
+    // LinBox backport of upstream v0.4.4 fix: for STATIC binaries (no
+    // PT_INTERP) RDX must be 0, not the exit bridge. The SysV process-entry
+    // ABI passes rtld_fini in RDX; glibc's __libc_start_main registers it
+    // with __cxa_atexit, and __run_exit_handlers calls atexit handlers
+    // BEFORE RUN_HOOK(__libc_atexit) (_IO_cleanup, the stdio flush). With
+    // the exit bridge in RDX the emulation ended inside the rtld_fini call:
+    // buffered stdout was never flushed (empty output) and the exit code
+    // became the truncated bridge address (128). v0.3.0 ends emulate() with
+    // Run(emu, 0); applying the same SetRDX(emu,0) right before it mirrors
+    // the upstream v0.4.4 placement (right after the Push64/SetRDX pair).
+    if(!linbox_hasinterp) SetRDX(emu, 0);
     Run(emu, 0);
     // Get EAX
